# Cloudflare Pages redirects/rewrites for the marketing site.
# Cloudflare Pages serves clean URLs automatically (/pricing -> pricing.html),
# matching the Railway Express `extensions: ['html']` behaviour.

# ── #560 — SHRINK THE SURFACE TO WHAT WE SELL ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Sixteen pages were reachable that no longer describe anything a buyer can buy. Every one is
# a page a buyer can land on from a search result or an old link, and a place a bug hides —
# which is the whole of #560.
#
# THEY ARE REDIRECTED, NOT DELETED, and that is deliberate: CORE-MAP rule 3 is founder-locked
# 26 Jul — *"nothing gets deleted"*. The files stay exactly where they are, so this is
# reversible by removing a line; nothing is lost and no history is rewritten.
#
# 301 (permanent) rather than 302, so search engines transfer the ranking to the page that
# replaced it instead of indefinitely re-crawling a page we have retired.
#
# Each target is the nearest page that still answers the same question — NOT a blanket bounce
# to the homepage. A buyer who clicked "Pipeline Calculator" wants pricing, not a hero.

# The engine is no longer sold as a standalone product (pivot locked 22 Jul: FIGSY is the
# engine under Milla&Vida, not a thing you buy). Its 73KB page sold exactly that.
/figsy            /milla        301
/figsy.html       /milla        301

# Nexus is the per-client learning brain: built, default-OFF and fenced (V2-TRACKER).
# Selling it on the site is ahead of the product.

# A status page with NOTHING monitoring production (#199 — the health probe exists and no
# monitor points at it). A status page that cannot tell the truth is worse than none.
/status           /support      301
/status.html      /support      301

# Overlaps support.html, which is the page we actually maintain.
/help-centre      /support      301
/help-centre.html /support      301

# A marketing calculator; pricing.html already carries the real one.
/pipeline-calculator      /pricing  301
/pipeline-calculator.html /pricing  301

# A cost-comparison page — the question it answers is a pricing question.
/vs-hiring-an-sdr      /pricing  301
/vs-hiring-an-sdr.html /pricing  301

# Company story lives on the homepage; the standalone page is not on the buyer's path.
/about            /            301
/about.html       /            301

# The Drop: a nine-page content/podcast series. Not the sell, and nine more pages to keep true.
/the-drop         /            301
/the-drop.html    /            301
/drop-01          /            301
/drop-01.html     /            301
/drop-02          /            301
/drop-02.html     /            301
/drop-03          /            301
/drop-03.html     /            301
/drop-04          /            301
/drop-04.html     /            301
/drop-05          /            301
/drop-05.html     /            301
/drop-06          /            301
/drop-06.html     /            301
/drop-07          /            301
/drop-07.html     /            301
/drop-08          /            301
/drop-08.html     /            301

# Unknown paths fall back to the homepage with a 200 (same as the Express catch-all
# `app.get('*')`). MUST STAY LAST — Cloudflare takes the first matching rule, so a `/*` above
# any 301 would swallow every one of them.
/*    /index.html   200
